<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 4.28 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 4.28 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian banks' internal credit</p>
<p>rose to 1,321.7 billion levs on November 15 from 1,267.5</p>
<p>billion levs on November 8, preliminary central bank figures</p>
<p>showed.</p>
<p>Credit to government rose 4.78 percent to 543.5 billion</p>
<p>levs, credit to state firms increased 4.12 percent to 353.9</p>
<p>billion levs and lev-denominated credit to private firms inched</p>
<p>down 0.61 percent to 130.8 billion levs.</p>
<p> PERCENTAGE CHANGE	  NOV15-NOV8  NOV15-OCT25 OCT25-SEPT27</p>
<p> Total internal credit	 +4.28	 +7.81	 +0.50</p>
<p> Credit to govt		  +4.78	 +8.40	 +1.09</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	 +4.12	 +7.96	 +1.05</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms -0.61	 -1.13	 -1.27</p>
<p> NOMINAL (BILLION LEVS)	NOV 15	 NOV 8	 OCT 25</p>
<p> Total internal credit	1,321.7     1,267.5	1,226.0</p>
<p> Credit to govt		   543.5	 518.7	  501.4</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	  353.9	 339.9	  327.8</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms  130.8	 131.6	  132.3</p>
<p> Dlr credit to private firms   1.11	  1.11	   1.11</p>
<p>(USD billion)</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
